<heading>events show - Inspect a single event.</heading>

<rule/>

<heading level="2">
Usage
</heading>

<pre>
  events show ID
</pre>

<heading level="2">
Description
</heading>

<paragraph>
Shows the full record of one event: its kind, timestamp, payload, and the
context envelope it carried — the actor, session, and command behind it.
</paragraph>

<paragraph>
The id may be abbreviated to any unique prefix (Git-style). If the prefix
matches more than one event, the matches are listed.
</paragraph>

<heading level="2">
See also
</heading>

<paragraph>
events list, man
</paragraph>
